---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Business Financing for Dubai Companies"
  description="Financing options once a Dubai company is established: business credit, invoice financing, and financing property purchased through the company."
>
  <section class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Financing</p>
    <h1>Financing your business</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Financing questions tend to arrive later than registration questions —
      once the company exists and is actually trading. Three situations come
      up most often.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Business credit and working capital</h2>
    <p>
      UAE banks and a growing number of fintech lenders offer working-capital
      facilities to established companies, typically requiring at least
      several months of UAE bank statements and trading history — this is
      not usually available to a company in its first weeks.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Invoice financing</h2>
    <p>
      For companies invoicing larger clients on delayed payment terms,
      invoice financing (selling the receivable at a discount for immediate
      cash) is increasingly available through both banks and dedicated
      fintech providers in the UAE market.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Buying property through your company</h2>
    <p>
      If the company itself is being used as a vehicle to purchase property —
      commercial or residential — financing works differently from a personal
      mortgage. See the network's property financing coverage for the
      specifics of buying through a corporate structure.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
